{"book":16,"chapter":1,"rubric":"FROM ASSEMBLER TO C / LANGUAGE BASICS / CHAPTER 1","slides":[{"title":"Assembler and C","sub":"Chapter 1 · Portable assembler","short":"Intro","main":"C is notation close to the hardware, yet portable: the compiler does the translating.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Assembler","C language","Compiler"],"captions":["Assembler: one instruction, one processor operation; the program is tied to one architecture","C: the same action is written in one line, independent of the processor","The compiler translates the line into instructions for the right architecture: RISC-V, x86-64 or ARM"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":100.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["lw   a0, 12(sp)","addi a0, a0, 1","sw   a0, 12(sp)"],"lang":"asm","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":190.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"three instructions for one x = x + 1","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":120.0,"y":74.0,"lines":["x = x + 1;"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":12.0,"lh":18.0,"w":130.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"one line, one idea","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":34.0,"text":"gcc","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":280.0,"y":38.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"RISC-V: addiw","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":280.0,"y":74.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"x86-64: add","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":280.0,"y":110.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"ARM: add","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":112.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":112.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":74.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":112.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":108.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[17.2,32.1]}]},{"title":"Four steps","sub":"From main.c to a.out","short":"Compilation","main":"Preprocessor → compiler → assembler → linker: every step can be seen.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Preprocessor","Compiler and assembler","Linker"],"captions":["The preprocessor expands the lines with a hash: it pastes in files and macros (gcc -E)","The compiler turns text into assembler (gcc -S), the assembler into object-file machine code (gcc -c)","The linker joins object files and libraries into an ELF executable and fills in the addresses"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"main.c","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":100.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"cpp","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":216.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":252.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"main.i","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"#include and #define expanded","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":40.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.i","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":70.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":90.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":120.0,"y":60.0,"w":54.0,"h":26.0,"text":"cc1","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":148.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":168.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":200.0,"y":60.0,"w":54.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.s","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":228.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":246.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":62.0,"h":26.0,"text":"as → main.o","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"addresses of other functions not yet filled in","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"main.o","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":80.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"libc.a","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":116.0,"y1":44.0,"x2":170.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":116.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":170.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":200.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":30.0,"text":"ld","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":230.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":262.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":308.0,"y":60.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"a.out\n(ELF)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[17.0,31.4]}]},{"title":"First program","sub":"main, printf, return code","short":"main","main":"main returns an exit code: 0 is success, anything else is an error.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["main and printf","Return code","Header"],"captions":["Execution starts at main; printf prints a string, return 0 ends the program","The returned number is the exit code: the shell shows it in $?; 0 is success, anything else is an error","The stdio.h header only declares printf; the linker adds its code from the standard library"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#include <stdio.h>","","int main(void) {","    printf(\"Hello!\\n\");","    return 0;","}"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":17.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":140.0,"y":56.0,"w":200.0,"h":56.0,"text":"$ ./a.out\nHello!\n$ echo $?\n0","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":300.0,"y":56.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"exit\ncode","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":250.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":254.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#include <stdio.h>","// stdio.h:","int printf(const char *fmt, ...);"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":100.0,"y":120.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"libc: printf code","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n~text","x":270.0,"y":120.0,"text":"added by ld","tone":"green","size":9.0}]],"cues":[16.0,25.9]}]},{"title":"Types and sizes","sub":"char, int, long, stdint","short":"Types","main":"Sizes depend on the platform; when they matter, use int32_t, uint8_t.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Integer types","Size in the name","sizeof"],"captions":["char is 1 byte, short 2, int usually 4, long and long long 8; the standard does not fix the sizes","stdint.h: int32_t, uint8_t and others: the size is in the name, as in Rust; signedness picks the instructions","sizeof is computed at compile time and returns the size of a type or variable in bytes"],"frames":[[{"t":"bar","id":"b0","x":60.0,"y":120.0,"w":36.0,"hh":11.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"1"},{"t":"text","id":"l0","x":60.0,"y":142.0,"text":"char","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"bar","id":"b1","x":140.0,"y":120.0,"w":36.0,"hh":22.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"2"},{"t":"text","id":"l1","x":140.0,"y":142.0,"text":"short","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"bar","id":"b2","x":220.0,"y":120.0,"w":36.0,"hh":44.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"4"},{"t":"text","id":"l2","x":220.0,"y":142.0,"text":"int","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"bar","id":"b3","x":300.0,"y":120.0,"w":36.0,"hh":88.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"8"},{"t":"text","id":"l3","x":300.0,"y":142.0,"text":"long","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["uint8_t   a;   // 0..255","int32_t   b;   // ±2·10⁹","uint64_t  c;","ssize_t   d;"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"lb / lw / ld by size","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["sizeof(char)    // 1","sizeof(int)     // 4","sizeof(long)    // 8","sizeof(int *)   // 8"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"pointer size = 8 on a 64-bit machine","size":9.0}]],"cues":[17.1,27.8]}]},{"title":"Variables and memory","sub":"Stack, .data, .bss","short":"Memory","main":"A local without a value holds garbage; globals are zero by default.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Local: on the stack","No value: garbage","Global and static"],"captions":["A local variable gets a slot in the function frame: its address is computed from sp (or it lives in a register)","A local with no initial value holds garbage: reading it is undefined behavior","Global and static variables live in .data and .bss (zero by default) for the whole run of the program"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int x = 5;"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":17.0,"w":100.0},{"t":"code","id":"a","x":150.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["addi sp, sp, -16","li   a5, 5","sw   a5, 12(sp)"],"hl":[2],"lang":"asm","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":200.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":280.0,"y":118.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"sp+12 : 5","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int x;","printf(\"%d\", x);  // ?"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":17.0,"w":160.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":280.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"sp+12 : 0x7f3a…\ngarbage","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"the result is random, and the compiler may not even read it","tone":"red","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":".data: with initial values","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":".bss: zeros","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"stack: locals","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":190.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["int g = 7;","static int n;","void f(void) {","    static int k;","}"],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":15.0,"w":160.0}]],"cues":[13.2,31.6]}]},{"title":"Arithmetic","sub":"Division, wrap, UB","short":"Arithmetic","main":"unsigned wraps around modulo, while signed overflow is UB.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Division and remainder","Unsigned: modulo","Signed: UB"],"captions":["Division drops the fractional part: -7 / 2 gives -3, remainder -7 % 2 is -1, the sign of the dividend, as in the processor","Unsigned numbers wrap around modulo, like a register: uint8_t 255 + 1 gives 0","Signed overflow is undefined behavior: the compiler may assume it never happens"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["-7 / 2    // -3","-7 % 2    // -1"," 7 / -2   // -3"],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":240.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"not Python's floor: -4 and 1","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":62.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":94.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":126.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":158.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a4","x":190.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a5","x":222.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a6","x":254.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a7","x":286.0,"y":52.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"p","x":180.0,"y":88.0,"text":"+ 1","size":11.0},{"t":"cell","id":"r0","x":62.0,"y":118.0,"w":30.0,"h":24.0,"text":"0","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell",