00beef\n 3.14","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":58.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"stdout buffer","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":270.0,"y":36.0,"w":150.0,"h":26.0,"text":"terminal: on \\n","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":270.0,"y":80.0,"w":150.0,"h":26.0,"text":"file/pipe: when full","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":122.0,"y1":52.0,"x2":194.0,"y2":38.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":122.0,"y1":64.0,"x2":194.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":132.0,"text":"fflush(stdout) flushes it forcibly","size":9.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[19.4,34.0]}]},{"title":"Constants","sub":"#define, enum, static_assert","short":"Constants","main":"Give values names and check assumptions at build time.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["#define","enum","_Static_assert"],"captions":["#define substitutes text before compilation and knows no types: parentheses around expressions are a must","enum defines named integer constants counting from zero: handy for modes and codes","_Static_assert stops the build if an assumption about types or sizes is wrong"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#define MAX 100","#define SQ(x) ((x) * (x))","int a[MAX];"],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"SQ(2 + 1) → ((2 + 1) * (2 + 1))","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["enum mode { OFF, ON, AUTO = 5, BOOST };","// OFF=0, ON=1, AUTO=5, BOOST=6"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["_Static_assert(sizeof(int) == 4,","              \"32-bit int required\");"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"an error at build time, not in production","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[11.1,27.1]}]},{"title":"Floating-point numbers","sub":"IEEE 754","short":"float","main":"Don't compare fractional numbers for equality; casting to int truncates.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Sign, exponent, mantissa","Comparison","Truncation"],"captions":["float is 32 bits: sign, 8 exponent bits, 23 mantissa bits; double is 64 bits and about 16 correct digits","Exact comparison of fractions fails: 0.1 + 0.2 != 0.3; compare the absolute difference with a tolerance","Casting to an integer drops the fractional part: (int)3.9 gives 3; if the number doesn't fit, behavior is undefined"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":50.0,"y":60.0,"w":30.0,"h":28.0,"text":"S","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":150.0,"y":60.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"exponent: 8 bits","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"mantissa: 23 bits","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"(-1)^S · 1.M · 2^(E−127)","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3          // 0","fabs(a - b) < 1e-9        // 1"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"the sum is 0.30000000000000004","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int a = (int)3.9;    // 3","int b = (int)-3.9;   // -3"],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"toward zero, like integer division","size":9.5}]],"cues":[15.9,35.6]}]},{"title":"Undefined behavior","sub":"UB and sanitizers","short":"UB","main":"For UB the standard promises nothing: the compiler optimizes the \"impossible\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["What it is","Optimization","Sanitizer"],"captions":["For some errors the standard defines no result: signed overflow, uninitialized read, out-of-bounds access, division by 0","The compiler assumes UB never happens and drops \"impossible\" checks: x + 1 > x becomes true","-fsanitize=undefined,address catches such errors at run time and reports the line"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":110.0,"y":36.0,"w":200.0,"h":24.0,"text":"signed overflow","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":110.0,"y":66.0,"w":200.0,"h":24.0,"text":"reading uninitialized memory","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":110.0,"y":96.0,"w":200.0,"h":24.0,"text":"array out of bounds","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":110.0,"y":126.0,"w":200.0,"h":24.0,"text":"division by zero, shift ≥ width","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":300.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":44.0,"text":"anything at all","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int f(int x) {","    return x + 1 > x;","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":200.0},{"t":"code","id":"a~code","x":230.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["li a0, 1","ret"],"lang":"asm","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":110.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"the check was dropped: \"always true\"","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":330.0,"h":56.0,"text":"runtime error: signed integer overflow:\n2147483647 + 1 cannot be represented in type 'int'\nmain.c:5:15","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.6,25.7]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: branches, loops and functions, and their assembler.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Program's path","Rules","What's next"],"captions":["Source → preprocessor → compiler → assembler → linker → ELF, which the processor executes","Types set sizes; unsigned wraps, signed overflow is UB; locals with no value are garbage; printf needs exact placeholders","Next: branches, loops and functions: how they become labels, jumps and stack frames"],"